cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fuel-lattice-ml: ML prediction of nuclear fuel lattice parameters"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the Materials Project."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Finney
    given-names: Cade
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-6335-1536"
    affiliation: "University of Florida"
    email: cadefinney@outlook.com
abstract: >-
  Random forest and gradient boosting regression models that predict the lattice
  parameters a, b and c of solid-solution nuclear fuel compositions from
  composition-derived features, trained on Materials Project DFT-relaxed
  structures. Retired: frozen at the version accompanying the manuscript, no
  longer maintained.
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-09-04"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/c-finney/fuel-lattice-ml"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22727667"
url: "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22727667"
keywords:
  - machine learning
  - nuclear fuel
  - lattice parameter
  - materials informatics
  - random forest
  - gradient boosting
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "The Materials Project"
    authors:
      - name: "The Materials Project"
    url: "https://materialsproject.org"
    license: "CC-BY-4.0"
    notes: >-
      Source of the training data redistributed as
      Data/MP_Dataset_Original_Trimmed.csv, which carries that attribution
      requirement. The trained models are MIT licensed, as is the source code.
